<title>USA: Brown Group to sell $100 mln in notes.</title>
<headline>Brown Group to sell $100 mln in notes.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS, Mo. 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brown Group Inc said Wednesday it signed an agreement to sell in a private offering $100 million in aggregate principal amount of its 9.5 percent senior notes due October 15, 2006.</p>
<p>The senior notes will be senior unsecured obligations.  </p>
<p>Brown Group said the notes will rank equally in right of payment with all existing and future senior debt.</p>
<p>The notes have not been registered under the Securities Act of 1933, as amended, and may not be offered or sold absent registration or an applicable exemption.</p>
<p>Reuters Chicago Newsdesk - 312-408-8787</p>
